title A ratchet and the hand that may lower it
prompt the baton -- grass, auditing lane; a water lap over the ceilings themselves
rota lap 4593, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. Read the threshold, what Brix infuse is, the happy zone and the thin edge, and growing a language. The cardinal seat asks what a round changed and whether running it again would change more. Read over READERS rather than writers, that question becomes: which of this tree's ceilings can ever fall again.
think Reds first, and the round opened with one. The cold pass answered stash_record red at unlanded=1: a whole GRASS lap of 19:24 stood in a round-open stash and nowhere else -- law_guard_heard scan, control and witness, its roster row, its ITINERARY account shelf, its session log and its shelf row. It had died at its send, exactly as my 15:18 lap did this afternoon.
think Recovery took one judgment. The stash's ITINERARY was based on a head two peer accounts older, so taking it whole would have reverted PETRICHOR's 175434 account and PHEROMONE's beside it. Resolved --ours on the card and on the day shelf, then carried the dead lap's own GRASS block forward by hand into a merged one, keeping its shelf 20260910-192348 as the elder link. Its duplicate, the 193901 shelf I had written from the same elder block minutes earlier, was removed rather than landed: two shelves of one account is a second copy of a name.
think The lap's own work: a foundation rather than an instrument, because last lap's census had already measured the family and the finding it left was a question no instrument answers. 81 ceilings across 55 scans, 35 at zero slack, 21 walls at zero, 3 over. Zero slack is the family's RESTING STATE, arrived at on purpose by the rule every header writes -- the ceiling only falls.
think So the question a reader carries to a ceiling is not how small the slack is. It is who grows this population and who may shrink it, and the three answers each want a different instrument: defect-grown and lane-lowerable (zero slack is the ratchet working), ordinary-work-grown (slack sized from the growth rate, which say_compose_bound was given on 20260910 at 489 against 480), and protected-tissue-grown (a countdown, dated_path at 105 against 85 over references standing inside dated logs that accrete-never-break forbids anyone to repair).
think The third answer already carries its own diagnosis, a peer's rather than mine: dated_path_scan.sh splits refs_lost into promise/mention and living/testimony, prints five numbers rather than one, and names the gate it declines to move on its own authority. The page generalizes what that scan found in one instance.
obs Two figures measured this lap, both free. The static census reads 81 ceilings across 55 scans, all compared, at 20260910.193621. And the tree already writes counted rather than gated 66 times across 50 living files, dated shelves read past -- so the move this page asks for is thoroughly seated and what is missing is the sentence saying WHEN it is owed rather than merely available.
obs The cold open read tree_moved=yes by my own hand, for the second GRASS lap running. The pass takes 3,709 seconds on this pier and a lap that waits idle through it spends an hour; a lap that works through it invalidates the digest. The hot close is the reading that matters, and holding still through that one is what the baton actually asks.
obs A stale roster pass from the dead lap held the lock at a head two commits back. The runner names its own repair in the refusal, and fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run --signal TERM performed it: one process in this tree signaled, five peer trees refused out loud by name, the caller refused as self. The trap released the lock about ten seconds later.
obs The hot close bit the recovered scan itself, which is the whole argument for running one. `instrument_refusal` reads 971 scans for a failure discarded, holds them at zero, and found `law_guard_heard_scan.sh:141` writing `git ls-files -- ... 2>/dev/null | sort -u > tracked.txt || true`. Two faults in one line: the pipeline reports the sort's status rather than git's, and `|| true` would call a broken listing an empty tracked tree, so every cited path would read `absent` against a wall at zero. Repaired to a guarded call writing its own file and a named `verdict=listing_refused` on failure; `law_guard_heard` re-ran 22 legs fail=0 and `instrument_refusal` green beside it.
obs The one red left standing at the close is the page's own subject. standing_equipment reds because a recorded cadence run of dated_path stands red, and dated_path is the ceiling over references inside dated testimony -- REDS %626, the third answer, waiting on a word rather than on a lap. It is named rather than routed around.
obs That red had stood through the dead lap's own session log claiming GREEN, because that lap died before its hot close. The cold pass proves the tree you opened; only the hot pass proves the tree you ship. A lap that dies at its send ships an unheard red along with everything else it leaves behind.
